{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,5]],"date-time":"2026-10-05T04:53:20Z","timestamp":1791176000233,"version":"4.1.0"},"reference-count":57,"publisher":"Wiley","issue":"4","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,7,14]],"date-time":"2026-07-14T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1783987200000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,7,14]],"date-time":"2026-07-14T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1783987200000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/doi.wiley.com\/10.1002\/tdm_license_1.1"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100001862","name":"Svenska Forskningsr\u00e5det Formas","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["2022\u201000959"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["2022\u201000959"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100001862","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100004722","name":"Stiftelsen Lars Hiertas Minne","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["FO2024\u20100400"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["FO2024\u20100400"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100004722","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":["onlinelibrary.wiley.com"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["Permafrost &amp;amp; Periglacial"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026,10]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>ABSTRACT<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>Permafrost in northern peatlands occurs within individual palsas or extensive peat plateaus and controls local carbon storage. These permafrost landforms are complex, and their internal structure remains poorly understood. We used quasi\u20103D electrical resistivity tomography (ERT) measurements, supported by UAV\u2010LiDAR topography, frost probing, and borehole drilling, to map the internal structure of two geomorphologically distinct palsas (dome\u2010shaped and plateau\u2010shaped) within Sweden's largest coherent palsa complex, Viss\u00e1tvuopmi. The results suggest that the 5\u2009m tall dome\u2010shaped palsa contains permafrost up to 20\u2010m\u2010thick beneath elevated areas, whereas permafrost is thin or absent in the surrounding lower\u2010relief areas on the palsa. In contrast, the plateau\u2010shaped palsa seems to contain widespread boulders, with the top of this material identified at depths between 3.8 and 5.5\u2009m below the surface, creating large resistivity anomalies and likely limiting frost heave. The permafrost base is difficult to delineate in the plateau\u2010shaped palsa because of the complex subsurface and limited depth sensitivity. Together, these results support the idea that palsas in deposits lacking boulders can heave into taller domes, whereas boulder\u2010rich substrates experience less frost heave and produce flatter plateau forms. This strong control of subsurface composition on permafrost structure highlights the need for detailed baseline knowledge, which is important for predicting palsa responses to future climate warming.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1002\/ppp.70053","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,7,15]],"date-time":"2026-07-15T00:00:57Z","timestamp":1784073657000},"page":"668-681","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Internal Permafrost Structure of Geomorphologically Distinct Palsas in Northern Sweden Revealed by Quasi\u20103D ERT"],"prefix":"10.1002","volume":"37","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-7775-1898","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Cas","family":"Renette","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Earth Sciences University of Gothenburg  Gothenburg Sweden"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Mirko","family":"Pavoni","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Geosciences Universit\u00e0 degli Studi di Padova  Padova Italy"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Mauricio","family":"Fuentes","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Earth Sciences University of Gothenburg  Gothenburg Sweden"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Erik","family":"Sturkell","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Earth Sciences University of Gothenburg  Gothenburg Sweden"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Mats","family":"Olvmo","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Earth Sciences University of Gothenburg  Gothenburg Sweden"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Heather","family":"Reese","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Earth Sciences University of Gothenburg  Gothenburg Sweden"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"311","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,7,14]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_11_2_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.5194\/bg\u201011\u20106573\u20102014"},{"key":"e_1_2_11_3_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1080\/04353676.1986.11880167"},{"key":"e_1_2_11_4_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1038\/nature14338"},{"key":"e_1_2_11_5_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.2136\/vzj2016.01.0010"},{"key":"e_1_2_11_6_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/2009JG001241"},{"key":"e_1_2_11_7_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/esp.1538"},{"key":"e_1_2_11_8_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.5194\/tc\u201011\u20101\u20102017"},{"key":"e_1_2_11_9_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/ppp.1951"},{"key":"e_1_2_11_10_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.5194\/tc\u201015\u20103423\u20102021"},{"key":"e_1_2_11_11_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1038\/s41598\u2010020\u201065719\u20101"},{"key":"e_1_2_11_12_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.5194\/tc\u201017\u20101803\u20102023"},{"key":"e_1_2_11_13_1","doi-asserted-by":"pu